node_modules/
# Build output. `dist*/` rather than `dist/` on purpose: the build flow renames
# dist out of the way before rebuilding (vite's emptyOutDir trips the Windows
# safe-delete guard on large trees), which leaves a `dist.stale-NNN/` directory
# behind. Listing only `dist/` let 202 KaTeX font/asset files get committed that
# way once.
dist*/
target/

# Test PDFs. Both trees are GENERATED, not authored:
#   test-pdfs/      -> scripts/make-test-pdfs.mjs   (synthetic fixtures)
#   test-fixtures/  -> scripts/make-fixtures.mjs   (writable copies; it rmSyncs
#                      and rebuilds the whole directory on every run)
#
# They used to be real IEEE papers. Committing them meant redistributing
# copyrighted material the licence does not grant, and 13 MB of weight for
# fixtures the tests only ever check structurally. `npm run fixtures` rebuilds
# both; `npm run verify:fixtures` proves the result is usable.
test-pdfs/
test-fixtures/

# Captured artefacts that reproduce a source document.
#
# The screenshots under evidence/ and test-artifacts/, and the annotated PDFs,
# were taken while the app was open on a real IEEE paper — so they contain that
# paper's title, author names, affiliation and body text, verbatim. Deleting the
# source PDFs is not enough while those exist: they are copies of the same
# content. Both are regenerated locally by running the app; what actually
# documents a claim is the RESULTS.md beside them, which is kept.
output/
test-artifacts/
evidence/**/*.png
evidence/**/*.jpg
evidence/**/*.pdf
# Shipped installers. Deliberately OUTSIDE dist/: tauri.conf.json embeds all of
# dist/ into the binary, so an installer kept there gets nested into the next one.
#
# The current installer IS committed, so the collaborator can install the latest
# build without building it. `release/*` first, then a negation naming that one
# file — without the blanket rule git would not descend into the directory to
# apply it.
#
# The version is spelled out on purpose. A pattern like `*_x64-setup.exe` would
# also match the twelve older installers sitting in that directory, and one
# `git add -A` would commit 65 MiB of them. Bump this line as part of the
# release; committing every version would grow the repository by ~5 MiB each,
# permanently, because git never forgets a blob.
release/*
!release/PaperAI_0.6.11_x64-setup.exe
*.local
.DS_Store
public/cmaps/
public/standard_fonts/

# Browser profiles. NEVER commit these.
#
# The CDP experiments used `--user-data-dir` inside evidence/, and those
# directories accumulated real profile data: Cookies, History, Web Data and a
# `Login Data` holding 267 saved-credential rows, plus the `Local State` file
# with the key material that protects them. 1477 such files were committed once.
# A fresh Edge profile has zero rows in all of those, so this was never filler.
#
# The catch-all is deliberate: a specific list is what let edge-serve-profile
# slip through while edge-ctrl-profile was covered.
*-profile/
**/*-profile/
Login Data
Cookies
Web Data
Local State
